{
  "fromId": "j_affricate",
  "toId": "dz",
  "preamble": "Fronting of the voiced postalveolar affricate [dʒ] to the alveolar affricate [dz]. Marathi has [dz] for the inherited Middle Indo-Aryan j (Maharashtri Prakrit ajja 'today' > आज /ad͡z/). The same substitution occurs in loanword adaptation: Modern Greek renders Turkish c [dʒ] as ⟨τζ⟩ /dz/ (τζαμί 'mosque', τζάμι 'glass'). Polish mazurzenie (dż [d͡ʐ] > dz) is filed under the retroflex cell ɖʐ → dz, not here.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Depalatalization, Fronting",
  "languageExamples": [
